WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.705
Start with a sine wave.

00:00:01.705 --> 00:00:06.170
Multiply it by the Legendre value, and take k to be a positive integer.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.415
Sigma is a signed integral.

00:00:08.415 --> 00:00:13.326
Integrate P sub n of cosine t times sine of k t, from zero to pi.

00:00:13.656 --> 00:00:16.730
The Legendre factor has magnitude at most one.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:20.719
The product stays between the upper and lower absolute sine envelopes.

00:00:21.049 --> 00:00:23.846
Positive and negative areas can cancel.

00:00:23.846 --> 00:00:28.582
The magnitude of the signed integral is at most the integral of the absolute product.

00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:30.791
Look at k equal to three.

00:00:30.791 --> 00:00:36.017
The upper envelope has three lobes, each of width pi over three and area two thirds.

00:00:36.347 --> 00:00:37.484
Count the lobes.

00:00:37.484 --> 00:00:42.706
For every positive integer k, the k lobes have area two over k each, totaling two.

00:00:43.036 --> 00:00:45.341
Every coefficient has magnitude at most two.

00:00:45.341 --> 00:00:49.202
This holds for every Legendre degree and every positive integer frequency.

